fix: add one-time trigger detection to session checkpoint

Reads stop_hook_active from Claude Code hook stdin input to detect
when this is a retry after a previous block. On retry, allows stop
even if issues exist (with "acknowledged" message).

This prevents the hook from blocking indefinitely when issues can't
or shouldn't be resolved before stopping.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

feat: implement session checkpoint command for stop hook integration

Adds kspec session checkpoint - a pre-stop hook for Claude Code that checks
for uncommitted work before allowing session end:
- Detects tasks in in_progress status
- Reports incomplete todos on active tasks
- Checks for uncommitted git changes (staged, unstaged, untracked)
- Outputs JSON for Claude Code hook consumption
- Exit code 1 blocks stop, exit code 0 allows
- --force flag to override and allow stop regardless

Closes task @task-kspec-session-checkpoint

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

spec: add session checkpoint command for stop hook integration

