feat: implement item CRUD commands with nested structure support

Add full CRUD operations for spec items that work with nested YAML:

- `kspec item add --under @parent --title "..." --type feature`
- `kspec item set @ref --status in_progress --description "..."`
- `kspec item delete @ref`

Implementation:
- Track _path in LoadedSpecItem (e.g., "features[0].requirements[2]")
- Add path navigation helpers (parsePath, navigateToPath)
- addChildItem() inserts into parent's child array
- updateSpecItem() modifies items in place via path
- deleteSpecItem() removes from parent array via splice

Items can be added under any parent item (modules, features, etc.)
and the type determines which child array to use (features,
requirements, constraints, decisions).

